# claudish protected terms: one term per line.
#
# Every word or phrase on this list is reproduced exactly in each rewrite: same
# spelling, same capital letters. Nothing here is ever read as a pattern, so
# characters like . + * [ ] are ordinary text.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments, blank lines are skipped, and a term
# therefore cannot start with #. Matching is case-sensitive, so add both
# spellings if you use both. A term may contain spaces. Limits: 64 characters
# per term, 200 terms in total.
#
# Copy this file, uncomment what applies to you, add your own, then run:
#   /claudish keep import <your-file>
#
# The examples below are commented out, so importing this file unchanged adds
# nothing. Keep the list to names: protecting an ordinary word like "plan" or
# "stage" makes every rewrite clumsy.
#
# Kubernetes
# api.example.com
# RFC 9110
# post-mortem
